    "Notes Updated": "8/14/2025",
    "Scouting Notes": "Advanced defender, works with a pitching staff well\n Love how he calls a game\n Receiving has improved and is pretty good now\n Shows a lot of positive emotion and leadership behind the dish. Gets great make up grades.\n Coming off torn labrum, the throwing is not where it used to be, and unlikely to ever get there. However, I still think this is an above average arm. Just not game breaking anymore.\n Swing can get long at times, but pretty good bat to ball skills. Shouldn't ever be a very high K% guy.\n Still chasing a ton, but still getting the bat on the ball a lot. Would really like to see some improvement in this department (and imagine the Brewers do too)\n Shows ability to hit the ball with power to all fields.\n Power is starting to return after his injury now too, some 107+ MPH HR in the last week.\n All Star level feels a lot less likely now, but still think he can be a very solid starting C in the league",
    "Notes Updated 2": "6/20/2023",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Reports say he is extremely mature for his age.\n Advanced defender, works with a pitching staff well\n Receiving isn't perfect, has some issues with low strikes at times, but for his age he is well ahead of most and is in one of the best framing development orgs in baseball.\n Shows a lot of positive emotion and leadership behind the dish. Gets great make up grades.\n Plus throwing arm that threw out 31% of stolen base attempts in a league that's rules favors baserunners tremendously.\n Swing can get long at times, but pretty good bat to ball skills. Shouldn't ever be a very high K% guy.\n Has some chase to his game. Bat to ball helps make up for some of the not great swing decisions\n Shows ability to hit the ball with power to all fields.\n Beginning to tap into power now. Not hitting as many ground balls.\n If the bat proves to be legit, can be a top tier catching prospect, league wide.\n In 2023, now has shown exit velocities up to 111 MPH. \n Potential All Star level catcher",
